MTM.schoolFaq = [
 ["What is the difference between British and American curriculum?","British curriculum (IGCSE/A-Levels) is more structured and exam-focused, with specialisation starting earlier. American curriculum offers a broader, more flexible approach with emphasis on continuous assessment and extracurriculars. British qualifications are globally recognised, while American curriculum typically leads to a high school diploma with optional AP courses for college credit."],
 ["How do I know which curriculum is best for my child?","Consider your child's learning style, future plans, and family mobility. British suits students who thrive with structure; American is ideal for those wanting flexibility; IB develops critical thinking and research skills; Canadian offers a balanced middle ground. Also consider where your child might attend university, as some curricula align better with certain countries' admission systems."],
 ["What are the typical school fees in Johor?","Fees vary significantly:\nBudget schools ($) range from RM13,000-30,000/year\nMid-range ($$) from RM30,000-60,000/year\nPremium ($$$) from RM60,000-160,000/year\nAdditional costs include registration fees (often one-time), uniforms, books, transport, and extracurricular activities. Some schools offer sibling discounts or early payment incentives."],
 ["Are there boarding options available?","Yes, several schools offer boarding: Marlborough College Malaysia (full boarding tradition from the UK), Raffles American School, and Forest City International School (Shattuck-St. Mary's). Boarding is particularly popular among families from Singapore or those relocating ahead of their families. Weekly and full boarding options may be available."],
 ["What documents are needed for enrolment?","Typically required: birth certificate, passport copies, previous school reports/transcripts, vaccination records, passport-sized photos, and proof of residence. Some schools require entrance assessments or interviews. International students may need student visa documentation. It's best to start the application process 3-6 months before the intended start date."],
 ["Do schools offer transport from Singapore?","Several schools provide cross-border bus services from Singapore, particularly popular schools in Iskandar Puteri. Journey times vary from 30 minutes to 1.5 hours depending on traffic and immigration. With the upcoming RTS Link, commuting will become even more convenient. Check with individual schools for current routes and fees."],
 ["What about special educational needs (SEN) support?","Support varies by school. Tenby Schools and some others have dedicated SEN departments with trained specialists. Services may include learning support, speech therapy, occupational therapy, and individualised education plans (IEPs). Always visit the school and speak with their SEN coordinator to understand the specific support available for your child's needs."],
 ["When should I apply and when does the school year start?","Most international schools follow either a September start (British system) or August start (American system). Some also accept mid-year enrollments. Apply 3-6 months in advance for best placement chances. Peak application periods are January-March for September entry. Waiting lists exist for popular schools, so early application is recommended."]
];

